      aboutWarehouseTitle: 'Warehouse type & door presets',
      aboutWarehouseText: 'The Calculate tab has a <strong>"Warehouse Type"</strong> field with 4 presets: Low-bay/Bulk Stacking, High-bay/Pallet Racking, ASRS/Automated, and Cold Corridor/Dock Staging — each preset auto-fills ceiling height, suggested floor area, evaporator/fan count, headcount, forklift type, door configuration, and typical lighting power density (W/m²) for that warehouse type. <strong>These are REFERENCE values based on common industry experience / real-world data the user provided, not mandatory ASHRAE/TCVN constants</strong> — always review and adjust to match actual project conditions after applying. For ASRS (typically very tall), the preset includes an estimated stack-effect infiltration item through the building envelope, calculated with the same Gosney-Olama formula but applied at full building height instead of door height. For High-bay and ASRS in rectangular shape, pallet capacity is <strong>auto-derived</strong> from the actual double-bay rack layout (1000×2390mm module/2 pallets, 3600mm aisle, 125mm flue gap, level count derived from height with 250mm bottom beam clearance, 1800mm level pitch, 2300mm top clearance to ceiling) instead of a generic area-density estimate.',
